From 3501dcf647e00c21012593f13048c14bfd3087f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mini <mini@local>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 03:37:37 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] Optimize GPUI Metal rendering, image/SVG memory, and
 idle power on macOS

- Bounds path textures to the area paths cover and double-buffers the layer.
- Wires shared CVDisplayLink to GPUI's frame waker (DisplayLinkFrames) so
  idle windows unsubscribe with zero vsync wakeups.
- Marks occluded CAMetalLayer drawables MTLPurgeableState::Volatile and
  forces presentation on restore if macOS purged a surface.
- Prewarms Metal shaders in an autoreleasepool with parallel pipeline
  compilation and a persistent on-disk MTLBinaryArchive cache.
- Decodes still bounded images via TransientBuffer mmap/munmap (clamping
  both width and height to 4096) with malloc_zone_pressure_relief, shares one
  lazy usvg::fontdb, clamps SVG height+width to 4096, shrinks arenas and
  instance buffers after spikes, evicts excess monochrome glyph atlases,
  defers ForegroundJournal's 4 MB ring until a collector attaches, and
  builds CGFonts off-lock in AppleTextSystem::add_fonts.
